# Line endings.
#
# Git on Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout by default. That would break
# `tests/test_source_hygiene.py::test_no_carriage_returns` on a fresh clone —
# the working tree would contain CRs the moment it was created, and the suite
# would fail before a single line of project code ran.
#
# Forcing LF also keeps diffs readable when the project is opened on Windows,
# Linux and inside the Docker images, which all touch these files.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files genuinely need CRLF: cmd.exe can misparse LF-only
# scripts, especially around multi-line blocks.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary — never translate these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.usd binary
*.usda binary
*.mp4 binary
